title:    While the grant is active
subtitle: A binding appears that nothing in the Terraform created.
width:    980
---
$ gcloud pam grants list --entitlement=folder-security-review \
    --folder=<FOLDER> --location=global --format="value(state)"
ACTIVE

$ gcloud resource-manager folders get-iam-policy folders/<FOLDER> \
    --flatten="bindings[].members" \
    --filter="bindings.members:jit-access-demo@<SEED>.iam.gserviceaccount.com" \
    --format="value(bindings.role)"
roles/iam.securityReviewer

# Nothing in main.tf creates that binding. PAM wrote it into the folder's
# IAM policy when the grant was approved, and will remove it on expiry.

$ gcloud resource-manager folders get-iam-policy folders/<FOLDER> \
    --impersonate-service-account=jit-access-demo@<SEED>.iam.gserviceaccount.com \
    --format="value(bindings.role)"
roles/compute.networkAdmin;roles/compute.viewer;roles/iam.securityReviewer;
roles/privilegedaccessmanager.admin;roles/resourcemanager.folderAdmin; ...

# The command refused in figure 01 now returns the policy. Same principal,
# same command, same folder - the only thing that changed is a 30-minute grant.
